{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-04T16:51:21.953Z","author":"claude-hub","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"259b6fa8d51ec5e6f7d340fb","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.317","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-memory-x47g"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Pool-lane stop test assumes the failing batch wins the first worker slot"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"test/worker-budget.test.ts 'one failed batch stops every pool lane from claiming further batches' failed on pm-memory#47 (release gate (26, npm), run 41858914984): '12 of 12 batches started after the first failure'. The assertion assumes batch 0, the failing one, runs before the other lanes drain the list. Nothing guarantees that: worker slots are shared by every test file under the same node --test parent (memory-worker-slots-<ppid>) and are won by 25 ms polling, not in claim order. While the property suites hold slots, lane 0 can keep losing the poll while lanes 1-3 run batches 1-11, so all 12 start and the assertion fails although the pool behaves as designed. #47 changes only tracker files, so the failure is independent of its diff."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["ci","flaky","test"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-04T16:51:21.953Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-04T16:51:21.953Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"claude-hub"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"The lane-stop property is tested deterministically, independent of worker-slot scheduling and runner load: after one batch fails no lane claims another, and lanes already running finish their batch; the real-process pool test keeps checking rejection and cleanup; runModelWorkerPool behaviour is unchanged."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"medium"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"5fd7e3a1df5b3780acc1ad14e650c35a2971971bac501eda58aa922ddb8761b6","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"c79c0f6d0ccd305b773433e4409f299f9f4f7c85c940a5aa08dc788bf475f5d7"}
