{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-04T16:53:07.568Z","author":"claude-hub","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"259b6fa8d51ec5e6f7d340fb","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.317","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-04T16:53:07.568Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-11-04T16:53:07.565Z","author":"claude-hub","text":"Fix: the lane loop moves out of runModelWorkerPool into an exported poolLanes(width, count, run) with identical semantics. A new test drives poolLanes with controlled promises: batch 0 fails only once all four lanes are busy, and batches 1-3 finish only after that failure is recorded. Exactly batches 0-3 must start, and the pool must return the one failure. It also checks that without a failure every batch runs once and that a pool never runs wider than its list. The real-process pool test keeps its rejection and cleanup assertions and drops the slot-order-dependent count. Revert check: removing the failures.length === 0 guard from the lane loop fails the new test. worker-budget passes 7/7 under Node and Bun; typecheck, lint, docstring, duplication and identity:check pass."}]}],"before_hash":"ffadbdcf999e8389ecacac524c256d1e18f23e524f674c277573a7baa0c0b79a","after_hash":"b8bd50272c02cf437d8367fc8c900896e7fcbbd0dac6e6a2fc914ffe7c93f783","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"535f58902bc7a224de5101da1f3fc95c03e8afb0532fd615dc4ffaa5d1b087be"}
