{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-04T17:13:32.194Z","author":"claude-hub","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"259b6fa8d51ec5e6f7d340fb","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.317","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-04T17:13:32.194Z","author":"claude-hub","text":"Review round 1 on 68e888e, both findings fixed. (1) CodeRabbit: the stop test recorded starts but not completions, so a pool returning while batches 1-3 still ran would pass. It now asserts that batches 1-3 finished before poolLanes resolved, and replacing Promise.all with Promise.race fails it. (2) Sourcery: a non-Error rejection went into the Error[] through a cast. poolLanes now wraps it in an Error naming the batch, with the original value as cause, and the test covers it. worker-budget passes 7/7 under Node and Bun; typecheck and lint pass."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-04T17:13:32.194Z"}],"before_hash":"3385f81f6cdec3b00bce2f148c300136e9c9eabd4ccc91423d85b744e16f05a7","after_hash":"9a72a95fff333cc212d775a494103accdf37dee530a44b191c17d4169b7da94b","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"413e4125c89c3a4e6c2ab4a6e9496e0c1e154eff6b9c1480b855e6d3901c28c7"}
